{{also|back-bite}}
==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|back-bite}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|bakbiten}}, {{m|enm|bacbiten}}, equivalent to {{af|en|back-|bite}}. Cognate with {{cog|is|bakbíta|t=to backbite, vilify}}.

===Verb===
{{en-verb|backbites|backbiting|backbit|backbitten}}

# To make [[spiteful]] [[slanderous]] or [[defamatory]] [[statement]]s about someone.
#* {{RQ:Conrad Heart of Darkness|page=213|passage=They beguiled the time by '''backbiting''' and intriguing against each other in a foolish kind of way.}}
# {{lb|en|informal}} To attack from behind or when out of [[earshot]] with spiteful or defamatory remarks.
# To speak badly of an [[absent]] individual.

====Synonyms====
* See also [[Thesaurus:defame]]

